    "result_text": "The full suite is green (only the acceptance test exists, and it passes).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `riskFlag` derived response field on owners, true when **any** of the three conditions hold.\n\n**Spec (`openapi.yml`):** Added a read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gets `get/setRiskFlag`), documenting the exact rule.\n\n**Computation (`OwnerRiskFlag.java`, new):** A self-contained helper `OwnerRiskFlag.of(repo, owner)` OR-combining the three signals:\n- **Possible duplicate** \u2014 reuses the persisted `owner.possibleDuplicate` (set by the existing `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`).\n- **Disposable-adjacent email** \u2014 the email domain shares a label with a blocklisted disposable provider (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`), e.g. `mailinator.net` or `sub.tempmail.com` \u2014 softer than the exact-domain hard reject in `RejectDisposableEmailDomain`.\n- **City over soft capacity** \u2014 new `OwnerCityCounts.overSoftCapacity()`: city already holds \u2265 40 owners (the existing `WARNING_THRESHOLD`), staying true up to and at the hard cap of 50.\n\n**Wiring:** Both single-owner responders (`RespondWithOwnerCreated` for POST, `RespondWithOwner` for GET) now set `riskFlag`, exactly mirroring how `capacityWarning` is derived at response time; `OwnerMapper` marks `riskFlag` as `ignore` like the other response-time warnings.\n\nA normal, fully-unique owner (no email, unique city, no duplicate) yields `false`, satisfying the provided acceptance test.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec's phrases \"disposable-**adjacent**\" and \"over its **soft** capacity\" name concepts that didn't previously exist, so I defined each in terms of the existing hard rules (blocklist labels; the 40-owner warning threshold) and documented those definitions in the OpenAPI description. If the intended thresholds differ, those two definitions are where to adjust.",
